## Findings: Base PWA Kit wishlist removal flow

**1. The remove handler** — `node_modules/@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/pages/account/wishlist/partials/wishlist-secondary-button-group.jsx:79-106`:

```js
const handleItemRemove = async () => {
    try {
        const promise = deleteCustomerProductListItem.mutateAsync({
            parameters: {
                customerId: customer.customerId,
                listId: wishList?.id,
                itemId: productListItemId
            }
        })
        onClick(variant.id, promise)

        await promise

        toast({ title: ..., status: 'success' })
        focusElementOnRemove?.current?.focus()
    } catch {
        toast({title: formatMessage(API_ERROR_MESSAGE), status: 'error'})
    }
}
```
This fires after a `ConfirmationModal` ("Confirm Remove Item") is accepted (lines 71-73, 134-138).

**2. The hook trace** — `deleteCustomerProductListItem = useShopperCustomersMutation('deleteCustomerProductListItem')`. In `@salesforce/commerce-sdk-react/hooks/ShopperCustomers/mutation.js:142-146` this calls the shared `useMutation` wrapper (`hooks/useMutation.js:28-41`):
```js
return (0, _reactQuery.useMutation)(authenticatedMethod, {
    onSuccess(data, options) {
      const netOptions = (0, _utils.mergeOptions)(hookConfig.client, options);
      const cacheUpdates = hookConfig.getCacheUpdates(customerId, netOptions, data);
      (0, _utils.updateCache)(queryClient, cacheUpdates, data);
    }
});
```
Only `onSuccess` is defined — **no `onMutate`, `onError`, or `onSettled`**. A repo-wide `grep -rn "onMutate" node_modules/@salesforce/commerce-sdk-react/` returned zero matches — no optimistic cache write exists anywhere in the package.

The cache patch itself (`ShopperCustomers/cache.js:219-239`, `deleteCustomerProductListItem`) splices the item out of the cached list via `updater: createUpdateFunction(list => {... list.customerProductListItems.splice(itemIndex, 1); return list})`, applied via `queryClient.setQueryData(queryKey, updater ?? data)` in `hooks/utils.js:30-35` — but this only runs from inside `onSuccess`, i.e. after the server confirms.

**3. Verdict: not optimistic — waits for server confirmation.** The item stays in the list/cache until the DELETE resolves; only then is it spliced out.

**Visible loading state: yes, a full-card spinner overlay.** In `wishlist/index.jsx:211-216`, `ProductItem` receives `showLoading={(...||deleteCustomerProductListItem.isLoading||...) && selectedItem === item.productId}`. In `components/product-item/index.jsx:60`: `{showLoading && <LoadingSpinner />}`, which renders (`components/loading-spinner/index.jsx`) an absolutely-positioned `whiteAlpha.800` overlay Box with a centered Chakra `Spinner` covering the card while the mutation is in flight.
